          "narration": "Welcome to this lab on apparent retrograde motion. Over several weeks, Mars normally drifts slowly eastward against the background constellations \u2014 here, across Scorpius and Ophiuchus. This slow eastward drift is called prograde motion and is the result of Mars orbiting the Sun in the same direction as Earth."
