          "narration": "After about two months, Mars resumes its eastward drift \u2014 as if nothing happened. The complete retrograde episode, from slowdown to loop to resumption, takes roughly four months and repeats approximately every 26 months. This cycle was one of the most important observational facts in the history of astronomy."
