          "changeMeaning": "The epicycle ring appears around Mars's current position and grows to show the small circular loop the geocentric model requires Mars to trace, with a yellow color indicating it is an artificial mathematical construct \u2014 helping students viscerally appreciate the complexity of the geocentric explanation.",
          "narration": "Ancient Greek astronomers, led by Ptolemy, believed Earth sat motionless at the center of the universe \u2014 the geocentric model. To explain Mars's retrograde loop, they invented a workaround: small circles called epicycles, on which Mars rides as it travels its main orbit. The epicycle traces out the observed loop \u2014 but it requires an extra mechanism added by hand for every planet. Notice how artificial this feels."
